{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790704114,"nonce":"E/HR7JMSkB3CQyLTT9U0cAtFDpE=","title":"Render nullable String values as \"null\" during string conversion","message":"Issue2716 fails on the tiered path when Std.string receives a null String from an array lookup. Both an explicit null element and an out-of-bounds element print an empty value instead of \"null\". The MIR String conversion path returns the raw null pointer, and the generic I64/String hint path bitcasts that same zero value without normalizing it.\n\nNormalize a null String pointer to the literal \"null\" at the String conversion boundary, including nullable String values carried through I64. Keep non-null values unchanged. Verify Issue2716, the authored regressions, and the full tiered conformance report.","files":null}]}